     1	# sealmap diagram corpus
     2	
     3	A hand-authored, citation-verified map of the sealmap workspace: one topic
     4	file per subsystem, each explained twice (for whoever inherits the code, and
     5	for the agent-harness owners who adopt sealmap), around Mermaid diagrams whose
     6	every mechanism claim cites `path:line` at the commit stamped in the topic.
     7	
     8	This corpus is **not** `docs/sealmap/`. That directory is sealmap's own
     9	generated, one-document-per-source-file output, checked by `sealmap verify`
    10	in CI. This one is written by hand with the `diagrams-as-code` method and
    11	checked by `tools/diagram-index-gen.cjs`. It catalogues the state of play and
    12	proposes no fixes; the register is the input to later work, not a plan.
    13	
    14	All topics are verified against `af4b8b4` (the tip of `main` when the corpus
    15	was written). Governing documents: [`docs/DESIGN.md`](../DESIGN.md) (accepted
    16	design) and the root [`README.md`](../../README.md). There are no ADRs.
    17	
    18	## Doors
    19	
    20	- **New to the code?** Read in order: MOD-01 (ids) → MOD-03 (the model) →
    21	  EXT-01 (the adapter pipeline) → COR-01 (the generated corpus).
    22	- **Deciding whether to adopt sealmap in a harness?** Read the "For the
    23	  business" sections of MOD-02, EXT-05, DEL-01 and DEL-02, then
    24	  [REGISTER.md](REGISTER.md).
    25	- **Changing the resolver or the walker?** EXT-03, EXT-04, EXT-05, and the
    26	  Debt rows from them in the register.
    27	- **Planning 0.2 work?** DEL-02 is the gap between `docs/DESIGN.md` and the
    28	  code; [DECISIONS-TIMELINE.md](DECISIONS-TIMELINE.md) is how it got here.
    29	
    30	## Areas
    31	
    32	| Area | Prefix | Covers |
    33	|---|---|---|
    34	| model | MOD | `sealmap-model`: the `sym:` grammar, hashes and fingerprints, the `Codebase`, sources, schema v2 |
    35	| extract | EXT | `sealmap-extract` plus `sealmap-rust`: the adapter pipeline, ids, flow walker, lowering and confidence, resolution, fingerprinting |
    36	| mermaid | MER | `sealmap-mermaid`: typed writers, escaping, injective diagram ids |
    37	| corpus | COR | `sealmap-corpus` plus the facade and CLI: generate, the index, projections, verify and write |
    38	| delivery | DEL | CI, the MSRV job, determinism, publication, and design versus code |
    39	
    40	## Checking and regenerating
    41	
    42	From the repository root:
    43	
    44	```sh
    45	node docs/diagrams/tools/diagram-index-gen.cjs docs/diagrams --check --cite-check --strict-citations
    46	node docs/diagrams/tools/diagram-index-gen.cjs docs/diagrams --check --render   # needs mmdc
    47	node docs/diagrams/tools/diagram-index-gen.cjs docs/diagrams                    # rewrites the block below, COVERAGE.md, REGISTER.md
    48	```
    49	
    50	`rendered/` is gitignored. When code changes, re-read the cited symbols at the
    51	new commit, correct the lines that moved, and bump that topic's
    52	`verified_commit`; leave topics whose sources did not change on their stamp.
